7 Minimal Node.js client

import { Client } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/index.js";
import { SSEClientTransport } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/sse.js";

const API_KEY = process.env.PAYGENT_API_KEY; // never hardcode this

async function main() {
  const transport = new SSEClientTransport(new URL("mcp.paygent.tech/sse"), {
    requestInit: { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${API_KEY}` } }
  });
  const client = new Client({ name: "my-agent", version: "1.0.0" }, { capabilities: {} });
  await client.connect(transport);

  const created = await client.callTool({ name: "create_card", arguments: {} });
  console.log(created.content[0].text);

  await client.close();
}

main();

Frequently asked questions

How does Paygent control agent spending?
Each card funds for exactly the amount deposited, with a hard cap set per account. There is no shared balance an agent could overdraw, and no card exceeds what was actually sent.
What are Paygent virtual cards?
Real, spendable card numbers issued automatically once a deposit confirms on chain. Each one is scoped to a single funding event, with its own number, expiry, and security code.
How secure are agent payments?
Your API key is a bearer credential scoped to one account. Card details are only ever returned to a request authenticated with that key, and keys can be rotated instantly from your dashboard.
Can I close a card and get funds back?
Yes. Calling close_card closes the card and refunds any remaining balance back to your wallet.
Does Paygent support MCP integration?
Yes, natively. Connect from Claude Desktop, Claude Code, or any MCP compatible client using the config shown above.

Notes

...

* Send any amount within the range returned by create_card , there is no need to specify an amount upfront.
* Sending more funds after a card is already active tops it up automatically, rather than creating a second card.
* Treat your API key as a bearer credential. Anyone with it can act on your account, so rotate it from your dashboard if it is ever exposed.
Questions or issues? Check your dashboard, or reach out to support.
